# Filament Authorization and Tenancy
- Policies are the single source of truth: they drive resource visibility, page access, and every action — register them; never substitute ad-hoc `visible()` role checks.
- `getEloquentQuery()` is the tenancy/IDOR boundary: in multi-tenant apps always scope it to the tenant/team/owner; an unscoped resource query exposes every tenant's records via URL id.
- All record resolution — edit/view pages, `Select::relationship()` options, global search, exports — must flow through the scoped query; never raw `Model::find()`.
- Bulk actions and RelationManager actions re-check the policy per record inside `action()`; a selected checkbox is not authorization.
- Hiding navigation (`shouldRegisterNavigation`, `->hidden()`) is UX, not authorization — routes and actions still exist and must be policy-guarded.
- Widgets, stats overviews, charts, and dashboard queries must apply the same tenant scope as the resource query.
- Never trust tenant/owner ids from form state; assign them server-side from the authenticated context.
- Tests must cover cross-tenant record access by direct URL and per-record bulk authorization.
